  m_Name: Template_strange_bonfires
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: DeadWalls::DeadWalls.CouncilTemplateSO
  Id: strange_bonfires
  Title: STRANGE BONFIRES
  Body: The horde's staging grounds lie exposed. Burning them is safe... looting
    them is not.
  BodyVariants:
  - "Fires on the horizon \u2014 the horde's staging ground, close enough to reach.
    We could burn their nests and buy a quiet night... or loot the camps first and
    risk waking them early."
  - "Scouts mapped the bonfire camps. Torching them thins tonight's assault. Picking
    them clean first is worth a fortune \u2014 if we're fast enough."
  OutcomeA: "The camps go up in oily smoke. Whatever was gathering out there scatters
    \u2014 tonight should be {NIGHT_PCT}% quieter."
  OutcomeB: "The crews strip two stockpiles before torching the camps. Both hauls
    reach the wall \u2014 but tonight comes {NIGHT_PCT}% harder."
  Contrast: 4
  OptionAAtomIds:
  - calm_night
  OptionBAtomIds:
  - wild_night
  OptionAVerb: Burn it all
  OptionBVerb: Loot first, then burn
  BaseWeight: 0.9
  MinDay: 9
